{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1692361792/5/codegen_prompts/9.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1692361792/5`\n- 题号：`9`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1692361792/5/9.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"9\">\n- `description`：网格中有一个被grey网格线分割成等大单元格的画布区域和散布在画布外的彩色瓷砖模板；每个单元格内的标记像素同时编码了要使用哪个瓷砖（通过颜色）和瓷砖的朝向（通过标记在单元格内的象限位置）。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为black。\n  - 网格中央有一个矩形画布区域，内部被等距的grey线条（1像素宽）分割为若干大小相同的方形单元格（例如每个单元格3x3或4x4像素）。grey线条构成水平和垂直方向的均匀网格。\n  - 每个单元格内部（grey线条之间的区域）恰好有一个非black、非grey的单像素标记点，位于单元格四个象限之一（左上象限、右上象限、左下象限、右下象限），其位置不在单元格的中心线上。\n  - 画布外部（grey网格之外）散布着若干与单元格同等大小的方形图案（瓷砖模板），每个瓷砖由一种颜色绘制（可包含该颜色和black像素的图案），不同瓷砖颜色各不相同，颜色集合恰好涵盖画布内所有标记点的颜色。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对画布中每个单元格，读取其标记像素的颜色C，找到画布外颜色为C的瓷砖模板。\n  - 读取标记像素在单元格内的象限位置：左上象限→使用瓷砖原样；右上象限→将瓷砖水平翻转（左右镜像）；左下象限→将瓷砖垂直翻转（上下镜像）；右下象限→将瓷砖旋转180度。\n  - 用变换后的瓷砖覆盖该单元格的全部内部像素。\n  - 输出中grey网格线保持不变，画布外的瓷砖模板被移除。\n\n- `Key insight`：标记像素承担双重编码角色——颜色选择瓷砖模板，位置决定瓷砖朝向。解题者必须独立归纳这两条规则：颜色映射可通过比对标记颜色和外部模板颜色发现，但朝向变换只有在多个使用同色瓷砖但标记位于不同象限的单元格之间对比时才能归纳出来。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/e734a0e8, eval/f560132c, eval/88e364bc, train/538b439f, train/84551f4c, eval/b10624e5, train/412b6263, train/e729b7be\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e734a0e8\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2849\nmechanism=0.3399\nlexical=0.0116\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:rotation, object:axis, object:marker, object:rectangle, object:template, output:same_size, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e734a0e8.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/e734a0e8.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nCopy the unique colored sprite tile into every tiled cell marked by an internal separator-colored pixel.\n\nInput structure\n- Full same-color separator rows and columns partition the grid into equal rectangular tiles.\n- One tile contains the only non-background, non-separator colored sprite.\n- Target tiles are otherwise background-colored but contain at least one internal pixel of the separator color.\n\nRule\n- Keep the separator lines and the source sprite tile unchanged.\n- Replace each marked target tile with an exact copy of the source tile.\n- Unmarked background-only tiles remain unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The internal separator-colored pixels are placement markers; the single colored tile is the template to stamp into those marked cells.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"unique colored sprite tile s in the separator grid\",\n  \"dst\": \"marked background tile d containing an internal separator-colored marker pixel\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"every marked d receives the same unique s\",\n  \"transform\": \"replace d with an exact copy of s, erasing the marker\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"f560132c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2830\nmechanism=0.3122\nlexical=0.0106\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:quadrant, object:rectangle, object:template, operation:reflect, operation:rotate, relation:between, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/f560132c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/f560132c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nAssemble scattered jigsaw pieces into a rectangle, recoloring each by a legend sprite's color map.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Several monochrome non-bg sprites (the \"pieces\"), scattered across the grid.\n- One sprite is the legend: it contains a multi-color k×k patch (typically 2×2) encoding output colors.\n\nRule:\n- Tile all pieces (rotations/reflections allowed) into a tight rectangle with no gaps.\n- The legend's k×k color patch defines a spatial color map over the rectangle.\n- Each piece is recolored to the legend-map color corresponding to its position in the assembled rectangle.\n\nKey insight: The legend piece doubles as both a jigsaw piece and a color key — its internal k×k palette assigns colors by spatial quadrant.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Assemble scattered sprites into a composite shape using a legend sprite that specifies colors for each component position.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"monochrome sprites scattered in the grid s\",\n  \"dst\": \"assemble into composite shape matching the legend sprite's silhouette d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.shape matches d.region.shape (d is always in top-left, final assembly forms rectangle)\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"s.color = legend[s.position_in_composite].color\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"legend sprite contains 2x2 colored pixels where each pixel's position (top-left, top-right, bottom-left, bottom-right) maps to corresponding sprite's recolor in final assembly\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"tight crop\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: identify legend sprite (contains multi-color 2x2 pattern); Step 2: identify other monochrome sprites with same shape structure; Step 3: assemble sprites into composite matching legend silhouette; Step 4: recolor each assembled region based on legend position mapping\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"jigsaw\",\n    \"color-legend\",\n    \"assembly\",\n    \"spatial-correspondence\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"88e364bc\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2839\nmechanism=0.3135\nlexical=0.0109\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:closed_region, object:marker, object:rectangle, object:template, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/88e364bc.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide yellow pixels inside walled regions in the direction dictated by border-legend arrows.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color; yellow pixels sit inside enclosed regions bounded by colored walls.\n- Border legends: small rectangles on the grid edge whose fill color C matches a region's border color. Each legend contains a center dot and an indicator dot encoding a direction.\n\nRule:\n- For each enclosed region, identify its border color C and look up the legend with fill color C.\n- The direction from the legend's center dot to its indicator dot gives the slide direction.\n- All yellow pixels in that region slide in that direction, stacking against the far wall.\n\nKey insight: Legend fill color links to region border color; the center→indicator offset encodes the movement vector.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Yellow pixels inside colored-border regions move in the direction indicated by the red pixel in the legend with matching background color, stopping at region boundary.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"yellow pixels inside colored-border regions s\",\n  \"dst\": null,\n  \"match_cond\": \"\",\n  \"path\": \"move(s, direction=legend.red_pixel_offset) where legend.background_color == s.containing_region.border_color until s.touches(region_boundary)\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"legend on grid edge with background color C and red pixel indicates: yellow pixels in regions with border color C move in direction from blue center to red pixel\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"legend/control-pixels\",\n    \"region-membership\",\n    \"directional-movement\",\n    \"boundary-collision\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"538b439f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2817\nmechanism=0.3227\nlexical=0.0111\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:axis, object:rectangle, operation:reflect, output:same_size, relation:between, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/538b439f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/538b439f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nReflect the solid rectangular source objects across the full separator line and color the gap with the separator color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background contains one full-width or full-height one-pixel\n  separator line in a non-background color.\n- One other foreground color forms solid rectangular objects, all strictly on the same side of that separator.\n- Remaining non-background pixels are scattered distractors.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the input grid shape and unchanged pixels outside each affected corridor.\n- Mirror each source object across the separator line.\n- For every source object, recolor the rectangular strip between the\n  original object and its reflection to the separator color, then paint the\n  reflected object in the source color.\n\nKey insight:\n- The full straight line is a mirror axis; the real objects are identified\n  structurally as the only solid rectangles confined to one side, while\n  scattered pixels are noise that may be overwritten inside the corridor.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"solid rectangular foreground objects all on one side of the full separator row/column\",\n  \"dst\": \"their mirror positions across the separator line\",\n  \"transform\": \"copy each source object by reflection; recolor the rectangular strip between each